            <div xml:id="d383">

                <pb facs="0347" n="337" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg337"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894A.00/5–1949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Taipei</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Edgar</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taipei</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-19">May 19,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received May 19—10:29 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>176. Provincial government and Taiwan garrison today jointly proclaimed martial
                    law here effective May 20. All ports closed except Keelung, Kaohsiung and
                    Makung. Execution for usual offenses.</p>
                <p>Repeated EmbOff Canton 39, Shanghai 141, Nanking 140.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edgar</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
